 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "avodah_zarah.39a.2",
   "daf": "39a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "וְטָרִית טְרוּפָה, וְצִיר שֶׁאֵין בָּהּ דָּגָה וְכוּ׳. מַאי חִילֵּק? אָמַר רַב נַחְמָן בַּר אַבָּא אָמַר רַב: זוֹ סוּלְתָּנִית, וּמִפְּנֵי מָה אֲסוּרָה? מִפְּנֵי שֶׁעֵרְבוֹנָהּ עוֹלֶה עִמָּהּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And minced tarit» fish, «and brine that does not have» a kilbit «fish» floating in it, and ḥilak are all prohibited. The Gemara asks: «What» is «ḥilak? Rav Naḥman bar Abba says» that «Rav says: This is sultanit,» a type of small fish that is generally caught before its scales have developed. «And for what» reason «is it prohibited?» It is «because its» size causes it to be «intermingled» with other fish, and as a result sultanit «rises» out of the water «with» non-kosher fish when «it» is caught."
  }
 ],
